    "result_text": "All 256 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `AcceptanceTest` and the existing `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests` (23 tests).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**Behavior:** When a request sets `sharesHousehold: true` and another owner already exists with the same (normalized) last name and address, the create is allowed instead of rejected with 409 Conflict. All owners in that household are assigned the same stable `householdId`, which is returned on the owner resource. Without `sharesHousehold`, a same-lastName/same-address owner is still rejected (409), preserving existing behavior.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `householdId` string property to the `Owner` response schema (drives the generated `OwnerDto` getter/setter, which MapStruct auto-maps).\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the persisted `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with accessors.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `household_id` column (tests run under `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the DDL is required).\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n  - Reworked the household check so a matching household only 409s when `sharesHousehold` is false.\n  - When sharing with an existing household, assigns a deterministic `householdId` \u2014 `UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes` over the normalized last name + address, so every member resolves to the same stable value regardless of creation order \u2014 and backfills the identifier onto pre-existing household members that lacked one.\n\nThe `householdId` is derived (not random), so it's stable and shared across household members without depending on insertion order, and it's non-blank as the test asserts.",
